{
  "evidenceID": "FOVEA-ORDINARY-IMAGE-W2-DIRECTIONAL-2026-08-05",
  "findings": [
    "All eighteen A-tier runs passed orientation, color and target-pixel hard checks with zero failed loads and zero hitches.",
    "In cold W2, Fovea and Apple each opened three origin requests and reused each original representation for three targets; Nuke, Kingfisher, SDWebImage and PINRemoteImage opened nine origin requests in this adapter/workload configuration.",
    "Fovea cold median was 34.654 ms versus 36.943 ms for Apple and approximately 131.7-141.5 ms for the four direct libraries, but this remains one directional Simulator workload rather than an absolute ordinary-image claim.",
    "Warm-disk exposes a real policy gap: Fovea re-decodes persisted original bytes at a 26.614 ms median, while Kingfisher and SDWebImage returned persisted processed variants near 3.6-3.7 ms and PINRemoteImage near 0.44 ms.",
    "Warm-memory Fovea was sub-millisecond at 0.293 ms median, but slower than Apple, Nuke, Kingfisher and SDWebImage on the same nine exact requests."
